---
// I1–I3: the summary, laid out as the ribbon is, in its two halves, one chapter per click, each with a small animation
// that keeps going by itself (no buttons: they only remind the room what happened); three directions beyond the
// thesis, one at a time in the middle of the slide: spatiotemporal modelling at BionamiX (groundwater, then a wildfire),
// influence maximisation, and inside artificial minds (a small neural network at work); and the close: the title's
// slogan over the cover's landscape, brought together, then its colours drained away and one flipped cell that sets the
// still life moving, and a QR code to the site (drawn at build time, no library at run time).
import Slide from './Slide.astro';
import SimButton from './SimButton.astro';
import { qr, qrPath } from '../../scripts/defence/qr';
const code = qr('https://michielrollier.be', 'M');
const qd = qrPath(code), qsize = code.size + 8;
// the summary's words are the ribbon's: its two halves and its four chapters
const halves = [
  { name: 'Getting to know the rules', items: [
    { ch: 'metrics', say: 'define and quantify LLNAs', act: 'rings', aria: 'A rule’s two rings with its Hamming weight and Boolean sensitivity, for one rule after another' },
    { ch: 'synchronisation', say: 'filter for rules that do what we want', act: 'agree', aria: 'The consensus-seeking rule bringing a rewired grid to agreement, from one random start after another' },
  ] },
  { name: 'Applying them', items: [
    { ch: 'network classification', say: 'understand rules that generate distinct fingerprints', act: 'prints', aria: 'Miranda et al.’s rule on the three networks, each with its fingerprint over it' },
    { ch: 'impact analysis', say: 'assign a dynamical importance score', act: 'stubborn', aria: 'The village with one stubborn person after another, and whether the village follows' },
  ] },
];
---
<Slide label="Summary" builds={4} class="i1" ch={0}>
  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <div class="i1-halves">
    {halves.map((h, hi) => (
      <section class="i1-half">
        <p class="i1-hname" data-b={hi * 2 + 1}>{h.name}</p>
        <div class="i1-pair">
          {h.items.map((it, k) => (
            <figure class="i1-item" data-b={hi * 2 + k + 1}>
              <canvas class="i1-anim" data-act={it.act} aria-label={it.aria}></canvas>
              <figcaption><b>{it.ch}</b>: {it.say}</figcaption>
            </figure>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p slot="say">To sum up, along the two halves of the research question, and the chapters along the bottom of the slides.</p>
  <p slot="say">Getting to know the rules. Metrics: we defined Life-like network automata so that every rule has its cousin, and worked out numbers and curves that quantify a rule before it runs, such as the Hamming weight and the Boolean sensitivity, here for one rule after another (Chapter 5).</p>
  <p slot="say">Synchronisation: with those metrics as a filter, we find rules that do what we want, here a consensus-seeking rule that brings a rewired grid to agreement, from one random start after another (Chapter 6).</p>
  <p slot="say">Applying them. Network classification: we understand which rules give networks distinct fingerprints, those that change their mind often, but not always (Chapter 9).</p>
  <p slot="say">And impact analysis: making every node stubborn in turn gives each a dynamical importance score. Here the best-connected villager, the most important one, a quiet one and another important one, in turn: twice the village follows, twice it does not, each time what that person does in most starts (Chapter 10, work in progress).</p>
</Slide>

<Slide label="Beyond this thesis" builds={4} class="i2">
  <h2>Beyond this thesis</h2>
  <div class="i2-stack grow">
    <div class="i2-item i2-st" data-b-only="0 1 2">
      <div class="i2-head"><img src="/demos/defence/logos/bionamix.webp" alt="BionamiX" /><b>Spatiotemporal modelling</b></div>
      <div class="i2-row">
        <div class="i2-gw" data-b="1">
          <p class="i2-sub">Groundwater flow</p>
          <p class="pub"><b>The MACCA-GW groundwater flow model: application to De Wilde Landen, the Netherlands</b><span>M. Rollier, L. Landuyt, J. M. Baetens</span><span>ACRI 2026, accepted</span></p>
        </div>
        <div class="i2-fire" data-b="2">
          <p class="i2-sub">Wildfires</p>
          <div class="i2-box">
            <canvas class="i2-firepic" aria-label="A wildfire spreading through a forest, cell by cell"></canvas>
            <SimButton class="i2-btn" />
          </div>
          <ul class="key"><li><i class="tree"></i>tree</li><li><i class="fire"></i>on fire</li><li><i class="ash"></i>burnt</li></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="i2-item" data-b-only="3">
      <div class="i2-box"><canvas class="i2-pic" data-pic="net" aria-label="The village of the impact slides, every villager coloured by how much they matter"></canvas></div>
      <figcaption>
        <b>Influence maximisation</b>
        <span>Many open questions, many relevant applications</span>
        <p class="ramp">matters little <i></i> matters most</p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="i2-item" data-b-only="4">
      <div class="i2-box">
        <canvas class="i2-pic" data-pic="ai" aria-label="A small neural network with random weights, passing one input after another through its layers"></canvas>
        <SimButton class="i2-btn" />
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <b>Inside artificial minds</b>
        <span>The same gap, with very high stakes</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <p slot="say">Where does this go next? First, at BionamiX: spatiotemporal modelling, where cellular automata model processes in space and time. Those need the extensions from the taxonomy of Chapter 2: rules that differ from cell to cell, more states, larger neighbourhoods.</p>
  <p slot="say">Groundwater flow: the MACCA-GW model, a cellular automaton for groundwater flow, applied to De Wilde Landen in the Netherlands, is accepted for the ACRI 2026 proceedings (with L. Landuyt and J. M. Baetens). It is not part of the thesis: a model in space, not a network automaton. Next to established models such as MODFLOW it offers simplicity, and many runs at once for ensembles.</p>
  <p slot="say">And wildfires, close to home: in August a fire in the Hautes Fagnes burnt some 3,000 hectares, one of the largest in Belgian history, and villages had to be evacuated. The picture is a wildfire as a simple cellular automaton, an illustration and not the BionamiX model, started with this click: green trees, red fire, charcoal where it has passed, a wind from the left; a burning tree burns for several timesteps and can set each of its eight neighbours alight, most easily downwind. Models like this ask where a fire goes next, and where a firebreak would help most.</p>
  <p slot="say">Second: influence maximisation. I wish I had started on node importance earlier: it holds many open questions and many relevant applications. Which few people, chosen together, reach the most? Does a stand-in rule pick the same people as the real processes on a network, an epidemic, an opinion, a product spreading? The claims of the impact chapter still have to be checked against such processes, and on real networks. The picture is the village of before, every villager coloured by importance, the most important ringed.</p>
  <p slot="say">And next for me: what goes on inside artificial minds. A neural network is also simple operations, iterated: every node adds up what comes in, each input with its weight, adds a bias, and passes the sum on only if it is positive (a ReLU). Here a small one with random weights and biases, started with this click, processes one input after another: dots carry what each link passes on, a node fills as it fires, and the largest output is ringed. Nobody writes down what a trained network does: the same gap between rule and behaviour, with very high stakes. The results of this thesis do not carry over directly, but the way of thinking, from the parts to the whole and back, can help.</p>
</Slide>

<Slide label="Thank you" builds={2} class="i3">
  <canvas class="art" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  <div class="i3-t">
    <div class="slogan">
      <p class="half top">The rich landscape<span>what we see</span></p>
      <p class="half bottom">of iterated simplicity<span>what we write down</span></p>
    </div>
    <p class="worlds" data-b="1">We brought these two worlds closer together.</p>
    <div class="thanks" data-b="2">
      <p class="ty">Thank you</p>
      <div class="qrrow">
        <svg class="qr" viewBox={`0 0 ${qsize} ${qsize}`} role="img" aria-label="QR code for michielrollier.be"><rect width={qsize} height={qsize} fill="#fbf8f1" /><path d={qd} fill="#0c2448" /></svg>
        <div class="col"><p class="url">michielrollier.be</p><p class="small">every demo of tonight, and the thesis chapter by chapter</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p slot="say">The title once more, in two halves: the rich landscape is what we see, the behaviour; iterated simplicity is what we write down, the rule. This thesis brought those two worlds a little closer together.</p>
  <p slot="say">Thank you. The colours drain out of the landscape, as on the still-life slide; then one cell changes, and the still life starts to unravel. The QR code leads to this site, with every demo of tonight and the thesis chapter by chapter.</p>
</Slide>

<style>
  /* the summary as the ribbon: two halves of two chapters each, every chapter an animation over its words */
  .i1-halves { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: calc(90 * var(--u)); margin-top: calc(24 * var(--u)); }
  .i1-half { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: calc(22 * var(--u)); }
  .i1-hname { font-size: calc(40 * var(--u)); font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); padding-bottom: calc(10 * var(--u)); border-bottom: calc(3 * var(--u)) solid var(--line); }
  .i1-pair { display: flex; gap: calc(40 * var(--u)); }
  .i1-item { margin: 0; width: calc(380 * var(--u)); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: calc(18 * var(--u)); }
  .i1-anim { display: block; width: calc(380 * var(--u)); height: calc(380 * var(--u)); }
  .i1-item figcaption { font-size: calc(34 * var(--u)); line-height: 1.3; }

  /* one direction at a time, each in the middle of the slide */
  .i2-stack { display: grid; align-items: center; justify-items: center; --tree: #4a7c32; --fire: #d8311c; --ash: #3d3833; }
  .i2-item { grid-area: 1 / 1; margin: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: calc(80 * var(--u)); }
  .i2-box { position: relative; flex: none; }
  .i2-pic { display: block; width: calc(672 * var(--u)); height: calc(672 * var(--u)); }
  .i2-box :global(.i2-btn) { right: calc(-24 * var(--u)); bottom: calc(-16 * var(--u)); }
  .i2-item figcaption { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: calc(18 * var(--u)); flex: none; max-width: calc(900 * var(--u)); }
  .i2-item figcaption b { font-size: calc(60 * var(--u)); line-height: 1.1; }
  .i2-item figcaption > span { font-size: calc(40 * var(--u)); color: var(--muted); }
  /* spatiotemporal modelling: the logo and the heading, then groundwater and wildfires side by side */
  .i2-st { flex-direction: column; gap: calc(36 * var(--u)); }
  .i2-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: calc(36 * var(--u)); }
  .i2-head img { height: calc(96 * var(--u)); width: auto; }
  .i2-head b { font-size: calc(60 * var(--u)); line-height: 1.1; }
  .i2-row { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: calc(90 * var(--u)); }
  .i2-gw, .i2-fire { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: calc(18 * var(--u)); }
  .i2-gw { width: calc(640 * var(--u)); }
  .i2-sub { font-size: calc(44 * var(--u)); font-weight: 700; }
  .i2-firepic { display: block; width: calc(500 * var(--u)); height: calc(500 * var(--u)); }
  .key { list-style: none; padding: 0; flex-direction: row; gap: calc(36 * var(--u)); font-size: calc(36 * var(--u)); }
  .key li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: calc(12 * var(--u)); }
  .key i, .ramp i { display: inline-block; width: calc(34 * var(--u)); height: calc(34 * var(--u)); }
  .key .tree { background: var(--tree); }
  .key .fire { background: var(--fire); }
  .key .ash { background: var(--ash); }
  .ramp { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: calc(16 * var(--u)); font-size: calc(36 * var(--u)); margin-top: calc(20 * var(--u)); }
  .ramp i { width: calc(220 * var(--u)); background: linear-gradient(to right, var(--panel), var(--accent)); border: calc(2 * var(--u)) solid var(--line); }
  .pub { font-size: calc(36 * var(--u)); line-height: 1.3; background: var(--panel); padding: calc(22 * var(--u)) calc(28 * var(--u)); border-left: calc(8 * var(--u)) solid var(--accent); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: calc(10 * var(--u)); }
  .pub span { color: var(--muted); font-size: calc(32 * var(--u)); }

  .art { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
  /* three states: the halves far apart; brought together (.together); moved up to make room for the thanks (.thanked) */
  .i3-t { position: relative; width: calc(1060 * var(--u)); height: 100%; }
  .half, .worlds { position: absolute; left: 0; transition: transform 1.2s cubic-bezier(0.6, 0, 0.3, 1); }
  .half { font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; line-height: 1.08; font-size: calc(84 * var(--u)); }
  .half span { display: block; font-size: calc(30 * var(--u)); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0; color: var(--muted); margin-top: calc(8 * var(--u)); transition: opacity 0.6s ease; }
  .half.top { top: calc(60 * var(--u)); }
  .half.bottom { top: calc(390 * var(--u)); }
  .worlds { top: calc(420 * var(--u)); font-size: calc(46 * var(--u)); }
  :global(.i3.together) .half.top { transform: translateY(calc(130 * var(--u))); }
  :global(.i3.together) .half.bottom { transform: translateY(calc(-110 * var(--u))); }
  :global(.i3.together) .half span { opacity: 0; }
  :global(.i3.thanked) .half.top { transform: translateY(0); }
  :global(.i3.thanked) .half.bottom { transform: translateY(calc(-240 * var(--u))); }
  :global(.i3.thanked) .worlds { transform: translateY(calc(-130 * var(--u))); }
  .thanks { position: absolute; left: 0; top: calc(420 * var(--u)); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: calc(18 * var(--u)); }
  /* a line that comes with a build waits until the halves have moved out of its way */
  :global(.i3) .worlds, :global(.i3) .thanks { transition: transform 1.2s cubic-bezier(0.6, 0, 0.3, 1), opacity 0.3s ease; }
  :global(.i3) .worlds.on, :global(.i3) .thanks.on { transition: transform 1.2s cubic-bezier(0.6, 0, 0.3, 1), opacity 0.6s ease 0.9s; }
  .ty { font-weight: 700; font-size: calc(72 * var(--u)); letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .qrrow { display: flex; gap: calc(30 * var(--u)); align-items: center; }
  .qr { width: calc(270 * var(--u)); height: calc(270 * var(--u)); flex: none; }
  .url { font-size: calc(44 * var(--u)); }
  .qrrow .small { max-width: calc(480 * var(--u)); }
</style>

<script>
  import { slide, sim, fresh, type How } from '../../scripts/defence/deck';
  import { stage, onSize, ticker, type Stage } from '../../scripts/defence/stage';
  import { decodeMosaic, mosaicPainter, drain, type MosaicJson } from '../../scripts/defence/mosaic';
  import { spark } from '../../scripts/defence/cover';
  import { ActiveLife } from '../../scripts/life';
  import { lattice, makeRng, build } from '../../scripts/net';
  import { type Rule, step, randomState, hammingWeight } from '../../scripts/llna';
  import { sensitivity } from '../../scripts/genotype';
  import { stepClamped } from '../../scripts/consensus';
  import { wildfire, TREE, BURNING, BURNT } from '../../scripts/defence/wildfire';
  import { TRIO, trioNet } from '../../scripts/defence/trio';
  import { picture, drawNet, type Picture } from '../../scripts/defence/netdraw';
  import { drawRing, type Ring } from '../../scripts/defence/donut';
  import { ridges, drawPrint, type PrintKind } from '../../scripts/defence/fingerprint';
  import { agreement, agree, WINNER, type Agreement } from '../../scripts/defence/agree';
  import { parse, mix, css } from '../../scripts/palette';
  import mosaicData from '../../data/defence/mosaic.json';
  import consensus from '../../data/defence/consensus.json';
  import clamp from '../../data/defence/clamp.json';

  // ── I1: the summary. Each chapter's animation starts with the click that shows it and keeps going, in a loop of its own ──
  type Act = { rate: number; reset(): void; advance(): void; paint(st: Stage): void };
  /** A grid of W × H square cells centred in the canvas; `fill(x, y)` gives the colour of a cell, or null. */
  function cells(st: Stage, W: number, H: number, fill: (x: number, y: number) => string | null) {
    const { ctx, t } = st, c = Math.floor(Math.min(st.w / W, st.h / H)), x0 = (st.w - W * c) / 2, y0 = (st.h - H * c) / 2;
    ctx.fillStyle = t.panel; ctx.fillRect(x0, y0, W * c, H * c);
    for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { const f = fill(x, y); if (f) { ctx.fillStyle = f; ctx.fillRect(x0 + x * c, y0 + y * c, c, c); } }
  }

  // metrics: a rule's two rings with its two numbers, the Game of Life, the consensus-seeking rule, then two rules drawn
  // at random, and round again, one every two and a half seconds
  const RINGS = (() => {
    const known: Rule[] = [{ r: 9, B: 8, S: 12 }, { r: 9, B: 488, S: 464 }];
    let k = 0, rule = known[0];
    const at = (i: number): Rule => (i % 4 < 2 ? known[i % 4] : { r: 9, B: Math.floor(Math.random() * 512), S: Math.floor(Math.random() * 512) });
    return {
      rate: 0.4,
      // a tile that starts playing advances at once, so it starts one before the Game of Life
      reset() { k = -1; rule = known[0]; },
      advance() { rule = at(++k); },
      paint(st) {
        // the rings and the two numbers under them, as one group in the middle of the tile
        const { ctx, t } = st, R = (st.w - 40) / 4, w = R * 0.41, top = (st.h - (2 * R + 112)) / 2, y = top + R;
        const rings: Ring[] = [{ x: st.w / 2 - R - 10, y, R, w, on: false }, { x: st.w / 2 + R + 10, y, R, w, on: true }];
        drawRing(st, rings[0], rule.r, rule.B); drawRing(st, rings[1], rule.r, rule.S);
        ctx.font = `600 30px ${t.sans}`; ctx.textAlign = 'center'; ctx.textBaseline = 'alphabetic';
        ctx.fillStyle = t.accent; ctx.fillText(`Hamming weight ${hammingWeight(rule, 8).toFixed(2)}`, st.w / 2, top + 2 * R + 64);
        ctx.fillStyle = t.danger; ctx.fillText(`Boolean sensitivity ${sensitivity(rule, 8).BS.toFixed(2)}`, st.w / 2, top + 2 * R + 110);
      },
    } satisfies Act;
  })();

  // synchronisation: the winner of the mission on the rewired grid of the race, from a new random start each time (one
  // that agrees within the thesis's 100 timesteps, as more than nine in ten do), five timesteps a second; it holds the
  // agreement two seconds and starts again
  const AGREE = (() => {
    const side = 30, N = side * side, net = lattice(side, 8, 0.2, makeRng(consensus.demo.netSeed));
    const start = () => { let s0 = randomState(N, 0.5, fresh()); for (let k = 0; k < 20 && !agree(net, WINNER, s0, 100).ok; k++) s0 = randomState(N, 0.5, fresh()); return s0; };
    let run: Agreement = agreement(net, WINNER, new Uint8Array(N), 100), hold = -1;
    const act: Act = {
      rate: 5,
      reset() { run = agreement(net, WINNER, start(), 100); hold = -1; },
      advance() { if (hold >= 0) { if (++hold > 10) act.reset(); return; } if (run.next()) hold = 0; },
      paint(st) { cells(st, side, side, (x, y) => (run.state[y * side + x] ? st.t.ink : null)); },
    };
    return act;
  })();

  // network classification: Miranda et al.'s rule on the three networks (two above, one below), faint, each with its
  // fingerprint over it, five timesteps a second from a new start
  const PRINTS = (() => {
    const rule: Rule = { r: 9, B: 170, S: 340, part: 'uni' }, S = 186, kinds: PrintKind[] = ['whorl', 'loop', 'tented'];
    let pics: Picture[] | null = null, a: Uint8Array[] = [], b: Uint8Array[] = [];
    const pic = () => (pics ??= TRIO.map((_, k) => picture(trioNet(k), S, 6, k === 1 ? 2 : 2.4, k === 2 ? 0.6 : false)));
    const lines = kinds.map((kd, k) => ridges(kd, 11 + k)), H = 150;
    // each print drawn once on a canvas of its own, at the pixels it is shown at: its fade towards the edge would wipe
    // the network under it
    let prints: HTMLCanvasElement[] = [], printScale = 0;
    const layer = document.createElement('canvas');
    const printsAt = (scale: number, ink: string) => {
      if (scale === printScale) return prints;
      printScale = scale;
      return (prints = lines.map((l) => {
        const o = document.createElement('canvas'); o.width = Math.ceil((H / 1.25) * scale); o.height = Math.ceil(H * scale);
        const c = o.getContext('2d')!; c.scale(scale, scale); drawPrint(c, l, 0, 0, H, ink);
        return o;
      }));
    };
    const ready = () => { if (a.length) return; const rnd = fresh(); a = pic().map((p) => randomState(p.net.n, 0.3, rnd)); b = pic().map((p) => new Uint8Array(p.net.n)); };
    return {
      rate: 5,
      // the networks are built, and a start drawn, when the tile is first drawn, not at page load
      reset() { a = []; },
      advance() { ready(); pic().forEach((p, k) => { step(a[k], p.net, rule, b[k]); [a[k], b[k]] = [b[k], a[k]]; }); },
      paint(st) {
        ready();
        const { ctx, t } = st, at = [[0, 0], [st.w - S, 0], [(st.w - S) / 2, st.h - S]];
        const scale = st.s * Math.min(2, devicePixelRatio || 1), imgs = printsAt(scale, t.ink);
        pic().forEach((p, k) => {
          // the network faint: drawn on a layer of its own, laid down at under half its strength
          layer.width = Math.ceil(S * scale); layer.height = Math.ceil(S * scale);
          const lc = layer.getContext('2d')!; lc.setTransform(scale, 0, 0, scale, 0, 0);
          drawNet({ ...st, ctx: lc, w: S, h: S }, p, a[k]);
          ctx.save(); ctx.translate(at[k][0], at[k][1]);
          ctx.globalAlpha = 0.45; ctx.drawImage(layer, 0, 0, S, S); ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
          ctx.globalAlpha = 0.9; ctx.drawImage(imgs[k], (S - H / 1.25) / 2, (S - H) / 2, H / 1.25, H); ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
          ctx.restore();
        });
      },
    } satisfies Act;
  })();

  /** The village (clamp.json) in a square canvas of any size, nodes coloured by `fill`, one of them ringed in red, drawn
   * last on a cream halo, over its neighbours. */
  function drawVillage(st: Stage, fill: (i: number) => string, ring = -1) {
    const { ctx, t } = st, s = Math.min(st.w, st.h), k = s / 700, pad = 20 * k, bx = { x: (st.w - s) / 2 + pad, y: (st.h - s) / 2 + pad, w: s - 2 * pad, h: s - 2 * pad };
    const X = (i: number) => bx.x + clamp.xy[2 * i] * bx.w, Y = (i: number) => bx.y + clamp.xy[2 * i + 1] * bx.h, R = (i: number) => k * (7 + 1.6 * Math.sqrt(clamp.deg[i]));
    const ringed = (r: number, width: number, color: string) => { ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(X(ring), Y(ring), r, 0, 2 * Math.PI); ctx.lineWidth = width; ctx.strokeStyle = color; ctx.stroke(); };
    const node = (i: number) => { ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(X(i), Y(i), R(i), 0, 2 * Math.PI); ctx.fillStyle = fill(i); ctx.fill(); ctx.lineWidth = Math.max(1, 1.5 * k); ctx.strokeStyle = t.muted; ctx.stroke(); };
    ctx.strokeStyle = t.line; ctx.lineWidth = Math.max(1, 1.5 * k); ctx.beginPath();
    for (const [i, j] of clamp.edges) { ctx.moveTo(X(i), Y(i)); ctx.lineTo(X(j), Y(j)); }
    ctx.stroke();
    for (let i = 0; i < clamp.deg.length; i++) if (i !== ring) node(i);
    if (ring < 0) return;
    node(ring); ringed(R(ring) + 9 * k + 2, 13 * k + 3, t.panel); ringed(R(ring) + 9 * k + 2, 6 * k + 2, t.danger);
  }

  // impact analysis: one stubborn person after another (clamp.json's cycle: the best-connected, the most important, a
  // quiet one, another important one), hand down and ringed, each from a start where they do what they do in most
  // starts; four timesteps a second until nothing changes, held two seconds
  const STUB = (() => {
    const RULE: Rule = { r: 9, B: 464, S: 488 }, n = clamp.deg.length, net = build('ba', n, clamp.edges as [number, number][]);
    const cl = new Int8Array(n);
    let k = 0, a = new Uint8Array(n), b = new Uint8Array(n), hold = -1, t = 0;
    const load = () => { const x = clamp.cycle[k]; a = Uint8Array.from(x.bits, (ch) => +ch); a[x.node] = 0; cl.fill(-1); cl[x.node] = 0; hold = -1; t = 0; };
    return {
      rate: 4,
      reset() { k = 0; load(); },
      advance() {
        if (hold >= 0) { if (++hold > 8) { k = (k + 1) % clamp.cycle.length; load(); } return; }
        stepClamped(a, net, RULE, cl, b);
        let same = true; for (let i = 0; i < n && same; i++) if (a[i] !== b[i]) same = false;
        [a, b] = [b, a];
        if (same || ++t >= 60) hold = 0;
      },
      paint(st) { drawVillage(st, (i) => (a[i] ? st.t.ink : st.t.panel), clamp.cycle[k].node); },
    } satisfies Act;
  })();

  const ACTS: Record<string, Act> = { rings: RINGS, agree: AGREE, prints: PRINTS, stubborn: STUB }, CHS = [5, 6, 9, 10];
  for (const s of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.slide.i1')) {
    const canvases = Array.from(s.querySelectorAll<HTMLCanvasElement>('canvas.i1-anim')), tiles = Array.from(s.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.ribbon .rch'));
    const tiles4 = canvases.map((c) => {
      const act = ACTS[c.dataset.act!], paint = () => { const st = stage(c); if (st) act.paint(st); };
      const run = ticker(s, act.rate, () => act.advance(), paint);
      act.reset(); onSize(c, paint);
      return { act, run, paint };
    });
    slide(s, {
      set(b: number) {
        tiles.forEach((t) => t.classList.toggle('cur', b > 0 && +t.dataset.ch! === CHS[b - 1]));
        // the tiles shown keep going; the others wait on their first frame
        tiles4.forEach((x, k) => {
          if (k < b) { if (!x.run.playing) x.run.play(true); }
          else { x.run.play(false); x.act.reset(); x.paint(); }
        });
      },
      enter() { tiles4.forEach((x) => { x.run.play(false); x.act.reset(); x.paint(); }); },
      leave() { tiles4.forEach((x) => x.run.play(false)); },
    });
  }

  // ── I2: one direction at a time. Spatiotemporal modelling: groundwater (build 1), a wildfire spreading from cell to
  // cell (./wildfire, started by the click that shows it, build 2); influence maximisation: the village coloured by
  // importance (3); inside artificial minds: a small neural network at work (4, started by that click). ──
  /** A small multilayer perceptron with random weights and biases (scaled by the number of inputs, a fixed seed): ReLU in
   * the hidden layers, the outputs as shares (softmax). */
  function perceptron(L: number[], seed: number) {
    const rnd = makeRng(seed), gauss = () => { let u = 0; while (!u) u = rnd(); return Math.sqrt(-2 * Math.log(u)) * Math.cos(2 * Math.PI * rnd()); };
    const W = L.slice(1).map((m, l) => Array.from({ length: m }, () => Array.from({ length: L[l] }, () => gauss() * Math.sqrt(2 / L[l]))));
    const B = L.slice(1).map((m) => Array.from({ length: m }, () => 0.2 * gauss()));
    /** Every layer's values for input x: the input itself, then each layer's ReLU(W·x + b), the last as shares. */
    const forward = (x: number[]) => {
      const out = [x];
      W.forEach((Wl, l) => {
        const z = Wl.map((row, j) => row.reduce((sum, w, i) => sum + w * out[l][i], B[l][j]));
        if (l < W.length - 1) out.push(z.map((v) => Math.max(0, v)));
        else { const m = Math.max(...z), e = z.map((v) => Math.exp(v - m)), sum = e.reduce((p, q) => p + q, 0); out.push(e.map((v) => v / sum)); }
      });
      return out;
    };
    return { W, forward };
  }

  for (const s of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.slide.i2')) {
    const fireC = s.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('canvas.i2-firepic')!, [netC, aiC] = Array.from(s.querySelectorAll<HTMLCanvasElement>('canvas.i2-pic'));
    const [fireBtn, aiBtn] = Array.from(s.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-simbtn]'));
    const fire = wildfire();
    let seed = 2026;
    fire.plant(seed);
    // green trees in three shades, red fire that darkens as it burns out, charcoal where it has passed, sand where
    // nothing grows; the greens, the red and the charcoal are the key's, from the CSS
    const paintFire = () => {
      const st = stage(fireC); if (!st) return;
      const cs = getComputedStyle(fireC), v = (k: string) => parse(cs.getPropertyValue(k).trim()), tree = v('--tree'), red = v('--fire');
      const greens = [css(mix(tree, parse(st.t.panel), 0.16)), css(tree), css(mix(tree, parse(st.t.ink), 0.2))];
      const flames = [css(mix(red, parse('#ff8a3d'), 0.3)), css(red), css(mix(red, parse('#4a0f08'), 0.5))];
      const ash = cs.getPropertyValue('--ash').trim(), sand = css(mix(parse(st.t.panel), parse('#b8955c'), 0.3)), { kind, shade } = fire;
      cells(st, fire.W, fire.H, (x, y) => {
        const i = y * fire.W + x, k = kind[i];
        return k === TREE ? greens[shade[i]] : k === BURNING ? flames[Math.min(2, Math.floor(fire.burnt(i) * 3))] : k === BURNT ? ash : sand;
      });
    };
    const burn = ticker(s, 12, () => fire.step(), paintFire);
    sim(fireBtn, 2, {
      reset() { burn.play(false); fire.plant(seed); paintFire(); },
      play() { burn.play(true); },
      reroll() { seed = (Math.random() * 4294967296) >>> 0; },
    });
    onSize(fireC, paintFire);

    onSize(netC, () => {
      const st = stage(netC); if (!st) return;
      const eta = clamp.eta, top = Math.max(...eta), lo = parse(st.t.panel), hi = parse(st.t.accent);
      let most = 0; eta.forEach((v, i) => { if (v > eta[most]) most = i; });
      drawVillage(st, (i) => css(mix(lo, hi, eta[i] / top)), most);
    });

    // the neural network: a new input every cycle, passed on layer by layer; while a layer passes it on, a dot runs along
    // every link, as large as what that link carries (ink when it adds, grey when it takes away); a node fills as far as
    // it fires, one that a ReLU stops stays empty; the largest output is ringed
    const LAYERS = [5, 7, 7, 7, 3], net = perceptron(LAYERS, 11), IN = 0.5, HOP = 0.6, REST = 1, CYCLE = IN + HOP * (LAYERS.length - 1) + REST;
    let tau = 0, vals: number[][] = net.forward(LAYERS.map(() => 0)).map((l) => l.map(() => 0)), inputs = makeRng(5);
    const newInput = () => { vals = net.forward(Array.from({ length: LAYERS[0] }, () => inputs())); };
    const paintAI = () => {
      const st = stage(aiC); if (!st) return;
      const { ctx, t } = st, lo = parse(t.panel), ink = parse(t.ink), R = 24;
      const pos = LAYERS.map((m, l) => Array.from({ length: m }, (_, k) => [70 + (l * (st.w - 140)) / (LAYERS.length - 1), st.h / 2 + (k - (m - 1) / 2) * 86] as const));
      const arrive = (l: number) => (l === 0 ? 0 : IN + HOP * l), shown = (l: number) => tau >= arrive(l);
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.5; ctx.strokeStyle = t.line; ctx.beginPath();
      for (let l = 0; l + 1 < LAYERS.length; l++) for (const [x1, y1] of pos[l]) for (const [x2, y2] of pos[l + 1]) { ctx.moveTo(x1, y1); ctx.lineTo(x2, y2); }
      ctx.stroke();
      // the layer passing its values on: a dot on every link, sized by |w · x| against the largest of that layer
      const l = Math.floor((tau - IN) / HOP);
      if (tau >= IN && l >= 0 && l < LAYERS.length - 1) {
        const u = (tau - IN - l * HOP) / HOP, carry = net.W[l].map((row) => row.map((w, i) => w * vals[l][i]));
        const big = Math.max(1e-9, ...carry.flat().map(Math.abs));
        carry.forEach((row, j) => row.forEach((c, i) => {
          const m = Math.abs(c) / big; if (m < 0.04) return;
          const [x1, y1] = pos[l][i], [x2, y2] = pos[l + 1][j], x = x1 + (x2 - x1) * u, y = y1 + (y2 - y1) * u, col = c > 0 ? t.ink : t.muted;
          // the link lit behind its signal, then the signal itself
          ctx.globalAlpha = 0.45; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x1, y1); ctx.lineTo(x, y); ctx.lineWidth = 1 + 4 * m; ctx.strokeStyle = col; ctx.stroke(); ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
          ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x, y, 3 + 9 * Math.sqrt(m), 0, 2 * Math.PI); ctx.fillStyle = col; ctx.fill();
        }));
      }
      const last = LAYERS.length - 1, best = vals[last].indexOf(Math.max(...vals[last]));
      pos.forEach((layer, li) => {
        const top = Math.max(1e-9, ...vals[li]);
        layer.forEach(([x, y], k) => {
          const v = shown(li) ? vals[li][k] / top : 0;
          ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x, y, R, 0, 2 * Math.PI); ctx.fillStyle = css(mix(lo, ink, v)); ctx.fill();
          ctx.lineWidth = 3; ctx.strokeStyle = t.ink; ctx.stroke();
          if (li === last && k === best && shown(last)) { ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x, y, R + 10, 0, 2 * Math.PI); ctx.lineWidth = 6; ctx.strokeStyle = t.danger; ctx.stroke(); }
        });
      });
    };
    const think = ticker(s, 30, () => { tau += 1 / 30; if (tau >= CYCLE) { tau = 0; newInput(); } }, paintAI);
    const blank = () => { tau = 0; inputs = makeRng(5); vals = vals.map((l) => l.map(() => 0)); };
    sim(aiBtn, 4, {
      reset() { think.play(false); blank(); paintAI(); },
      play() { if (!vals[0].some(Boolean)) newInput(); think.play(true); },
    });
    onSize(aiC, paintAI);

    slide(s, {
      // a direction that leaves the slide stops; the fire picks up again when a step back returns to it
      set(b: number, how: How) {
        if (b !== 2) burn.play(false); else if (how === 'prev' && fireBtn.dataset.run) burn.play(true);
        if (b < 4) think.play(false);
      },
      leave() { burn.play(false); think.play(false); },
    });
  }

  // ── I3: the slogan's two halves come together over the landscape; then thanks, the colours drain away as on slide
  // C3, and once they are gone one flipped cell sets the still life moving ──
  const m = decodeMosaic(mosaicData as MosaicJson);
  // the flipped cell: a live cell near a point in the big tiles on the right of the page, one whose loss spreads
  const flip = spark(m.live, m.PW, m.PH, 0.8 * m.W + m.M, 0.5 * m.H + m.M);
  for (const s of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.slide.i3')) {
    const c = s.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('canvas.art')!, draw = mosaicPainter(m, '#0c2448', getComputedStyle(c).getPropertyValue('--bg').trim());
    let live = m.live.slice(), life = new ActiveLife(m.PW, m.PH), gens = 0, stop = () => {};
    const reset = () => { live = m.live.slice(); life = new ActiveLife(m.PW, m.PH); gens = 0; };
    const paint = () => { const st = stage(c); if (st) draw(st.ctx, live, 0, 0, st.w, st.h); };
    const run = ticker(s, 10, () => { gens++; return life.step(live) === 0; }, paint);
    const go = () => { live[flip] ^= 1; life.touch(flip % m.PW, Math.floor(flip / m.PW)); run.play(true); };
    slide(s, {
      set(b: number, how: How) {
        s.classList.toggle('together', b >= 1); s.classList.toggle('thanked', b >= 2);
        if (b < 2) { stop(); run.play(false); reset(); draw.plain.fill(0); }
        else if (how === 'next') { stop(); reset(); draw.plain.fill(0); stop = drain(draw, [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], paint, go); }
        else if (gens === 0) { stop(); reset(); draw.plain.fill(1); go(); }
        paint();
      },
      enter() { stop(); reset(); draw.plain.fill(0); },
      leave() { stop(); run.play(false); },
    });
    onSize(c, paint);
  }
</script>
